WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.060
Dim Sum Rush. A partnership climbing game

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.700
where you help your partner through the face-up tiles you share.

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.570
You win or lose as a team, so every pass is a chance to set your partner up.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.630
Lead a single, a set like five-five, or a run like three-four-five.

5
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.450
Others must follow with the same kind and size,

6
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.770
of equal or higher ranks, or pass.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.710
You can't rearrange your hand.

8
00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.370
Teammates help you through the trolley you both share:

9
00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:30.010
when you pass, swap an end tile for one of the trolley tiles,

10
00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.820
and slide it in anywhere in your hand.

11
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.570
Teams sit alternating.

12
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.580
Everyone on the team must empty their hands to win the round.

13
00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.760
Let's take a look at the game played.

14
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.870
I lead three-four-five from my hand. Bao beats it.

15
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.490
My partner passes, putting out an eight.

16
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.890
I pass and swap the two at the end of my hand for her eight.

17
00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.490
She goes out on three tens.

18
00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.140
Six to nine from my hand: a Chef's Special,

19
00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.950
or a bomb, which beats any ordinary play.

20
00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.590
Our side is out, so their team takes penalty points.

21
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.410
The best moments are like that one:

22
00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.060
your partner leaves you exactly the tile you needed,

23
00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.590
and a Special comes out of nowhere.

24
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.270
The free-for-all mode allows players to share

25
00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:15.010
a single trolley with all their opponents,

26
00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.930
allowing them to be able to swap with any trolley tile on the table.

27
00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.030
The first one to shed ends the round, scoring zero,

28
00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.080
and everyone else scores penalty points

29
00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.110
based on the number of tiles left in their hand.

30
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.700
Two to six players, thirty to forty-five minutes. Seventy-two tiles or cards.

31
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.660
The fewest penalties after three rounds wins.

32
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.530
Dim Sum Rush. Play it in your browser at darrendon.com,

33
00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.080
or email me for a prototype.
